# Copy to .env in the repo root and edit. Both scripts/run/env.sh (the shell commands) and
# src/repo_paths.py (every python script) read it; a variable already set in the
# environment wins over .env. Plain KEY=value lines, no quotes, no spaces around '='.
# Nothing here is needed to rebuild the paper (`make paper`) or run the gates (`make check`).

# Required for data preparation, training, evaluation and the GPU analyses.
# Tokenized corpus: <root>/data/fineweb-edu-100bt/{train,val}.bin (~54 GB) and the
# Hugging Face download cache <root>/.hf_cache used while preparing it.
DUALSPS_DATA_ROOT=/path/to/dualsps

# Run outputs: checkpoints in <root>/out/<run>/, and the live evaluation ledger and
# wall-clock rows in <root>/results/. Default: DUALSPS_DATA_ROOT.
# DUALSPS_OUT_ROOT=/path/to/dualsps

# Python environment used by scripts/run/env.sh. Default: <repo>/.venv (uv sync).
# VENV=/path/to/.venv

# Hugging Face model repo holding the checkpoints (scripts/dualsps/hf_export.py only).
# Default: ryankim17920/mechanistic-sps, the public repo of the paper's checkpoints
# (downloads need no login).
# DUALSPS_HF_REPO=ryankim17920/mechanistic-sps

# Logs of the training runs (README, "Training"); eval_runs.py reads throughput and
# wall-clock from them. Default: <DUALSPS_DATA_ROOT>/logs.
# DUALSPS_LOG_DIR=/path/to/logs
